<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:54:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Russia renews Kyiv strikes after three-day pause</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe35448d8c8cc82305f4beab785f9ca1fef962ac6218a1ed02d1796fc5a026c6</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:52:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T02:00:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt--c216aa8a2eec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt" /><summary type="html">Russia resumed strikes on Kyiv late Monday after a three-day pause ordered by President Vladimir Putin expired, Ukraine’s emergency service said. The halt coincided with visits to Moscow and Kyiv by US President Donald Trump’s envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner, who were holding talks aimed at ending the war. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU says no place for 'glorification of war criminals' as Mladic buried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2962da943164fdf754d383cbf2d7e292866a417a3c24558ca17fad42102eb946</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:52:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T21:35:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-says-no-place-for-glorification-of-war-criminals-as-mladic-buried--c505261200fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-no-place-for-glorification-of-war-criminals-as-mladic-buried" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Monday denounced any "glorification" of convicted war criminal Ratko Mladic in Serbia, as thousands gathered in Belgrade for his funeral. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Only the beginning? German far-right's breakthrough shakes Europe to its core</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:687ebf409debbaae8d899780ce13e0724d49e9df0ae57564afa75f846c6a7b5f</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:53:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T19:38:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260907-only-the-beginning-german-far-right-s-breakthrough-shakes-europe-to-its-core--984465a67934.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260907-only-the-beginning-german-far-right-s-breakthrough-shakes-europe-to-its-core" /><summary type="html">Not enough to win outright but enough to shake Germany and Europe to their core: the far-right Alterniv für Deutschland trouncing the ruling conservatives in the impoverished former East German region of Saxony-Anhalt. We’ll ask about the consequences of voting for an anti-immigrant, pro-Russian party that wants schools to teach less about the ills of Hitler and more the glory of Bismarck.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'What we see right now is that Putin has zero interest in ending the war', Ukrainian MP Yasko says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecc3fdd634b2abd2e79b1a59b31241e4567485b33bbc28b5343a614f39c88b3b</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:53:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:38:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says--3db6e994afb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says" /><summary type="html">US envoy Steve Witkoff on Monday touted progress in weekend discussions with Ukraine and Russia, raising the prospect of reviving three-way peace talks to end Europe's deadliest conflict since World War II. Ukrainian MP Lisa Yasko says that "we don't trust these talks", describing the US envoys' flattery towards Russian President Vladimir Putin as "disgraceful".</summary></entry><entry><title>Avalanche kills at least 11 climbers in southern Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89330cbc6455ebfbd506518d4dfcbf6e510f4a9b6ff6ce126b2156639a3e1b08</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:53:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:00:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia--cc82d0868712.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia" /><summary type="html">⁠At least ​11 people were killed and six ​others injured after an avalanche struck a group of climbers in Russia's ​southern Kabardino-Balkaria ‌Republic, local emergency services said. The ‌avalanche swept down Mount Mizhirgi, ⁠one of the highest peaks in Russia's North Caucasus.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1d32ecce8d2d57fab5a5f5dad1c1bdcea59ce189e78700cf085b45060252fb1</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:53:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1--3d84be7d1802.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1" /><summary type="html">Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.</summary></entry><entry><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75eb937a1f1117856993f7fdd435e4acadcc86ab7a246882d0a037d55b75e48c</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:45:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd--3acc1083cc66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd" /><summary type="html">Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa12b7441f4df1b59bb3a7d4739682df6eaaa5e39b86f524c1d3a431cc7488d0</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:53:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1--355f2ad6ae17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Jubilation and pain': German far right marches to victory in key state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37c4359633fbee2c6ef5e3634c5bc41b9b8399d6b5b7447acda675e7c3d9db13</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:05:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election--1210a591a6c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 7: The far right marches to victory in a German state election: what does this mean for the future of Germany and Europe at large? Also: the Daily Telegraph publishes an exclusive interview with the sons of former Pakistani PM Imran Khan about his imprisonment conditions in Pakistan. Plus the US Open descends into chaos after influencers, weed and disruptions stir controversy.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks to dismiss Nicaragua's Gaza genocide case at top UN court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6860c4a98adcbb3563404bce6bee2667f7bc91c5c480941a80225d1987e6734c</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:54:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:14:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court--eec11aeeb4e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court" /><summary type="html">Germany is set to ask the International Court of Justice on Monday to dismiss a case accusing Berlin of "facilitating genocide" in Gaza by supporting Israel after the deadly October 7, 2023 attacks by Hamas militants. The details of the case, filed by Nicaragua in 2024, have not yet been made public.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of mourners gather in Belgrade for war criminal Mladic's funeral</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61c59f63fe9f4797cb9cfb8022866c51eb0edf6f04b05a2edd89355109485c1b</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:54:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T08:08:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-thousands-of-mourners-gather-in-belgrade-for-war-criminal-mladic-s-funeral--0ff58bef6eca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-thousands-of-mourners-gather-in-belgrade-for-war-criminal-mladic-s-funeral" /><summary type="html">Thousands of mourners on Monday gathered at a church in Belgrade for the funeral of Ratko Mladic, who died in The Hague, Netherlands, on August 27 while serving a life sentence for genocide, war crimes and crimes against humanity. The European Union heavily criticised the decision to hold a public funeral service with Marta Kos, the bloc's enlargement commissioner, having cancelled an upcoming visit to Serbia in protest.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Merz 'deeply shocked' by far-right AfD's historic electoral victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cb636323073432f074b21b0033bcb42cdba4836a4aedb2971ef0f9c0bdf7d58</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:54:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T06:30:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-live-europe-reacts-to-germany-far-right-afd-worrying-electoral-victory--3bd65a3dc7ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-live-europe-reacts-to-germany-far-right-afd-worrying-electoral-victory" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz told the press on Monday that he was "deeply shocked" by the far-right AfD's historic victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election a day earlier. The AfD is labelled a "right-wing extremist" group by Germany's domestic intelligence agency, and some of its staff are former members of a since-banned neo-Nazi organisation. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz vows to stick with reforms despite election drubbing by far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51443c546e12a7c49342a36a6a572056c2ed876228cd0568e883f31c8ffbbfe0</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:54:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T05:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-s-merz-shocked-by-far-right-state-win-but-vows-to-stay-course--601c526382cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-s-merz-shocked-by-far-right-state-win-but-vows-to-stay-course" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Monday vowed to press ahead with his reform agenda despite a blistering election defeat for his centre-right CDU in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right AfD won almost 44 percent of the vote. Merz called the result his party’s worst defeat in decades.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys bring ‘more effective’ Ukraine peace proposals to Kyiv, official says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8270d94f6332a3d7af07c5ad6f559b0ff2b14d34437f4447cc846e513fd898fb</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:31:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv--37419914ba3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv" /><summary type="html">US envoys brought new, “more effective” proposals to Kyiv aimed at ending the war with Russia, a senior Ukrainian presidential official said on Sunday. President Volodymyr Zelensky and US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner described talks positively but announced no breakthrough, as Zelensky warned fighting could continue into winter.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU to boost Greenland investment amid Trump annexation claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5633faefd886062bd1cfd7cc35fd0f5c72e960eaf6079579b9d5bffce3525c1a</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:27:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation--2b5a527b0c9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen is expected to announce increased EU investment in Greenland on Monday, including in critical minerals, satellite communications and renewable energy. Her two-day visit signals support for Greenland and Denmark amid US President Donald Trump’s push for American control of the Arctic territory.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Ready to talk': German far right celebrates victory in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8984badb6b30e39499d035c941fb5c2744e47203f8cc34be34eca50736d4ee64</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T17:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory--e252fd4fc28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory" /><summary type="html">"Everything is possible" was the campaign slogan of the Alternative for Germany (AfD) in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right party has won a landslide election victory, although they appear short of a majority in the state parliament. Ulrich Siegmund, who is in pole position to become the state leader, knows he has history in his grasp. We get reaction from CSU MP Tobias Winkler.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s far-right AfD wins big in key state election but falls short of majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:422bd17db10e9f2725ed10e1802ffad4caf58e5f194e6218471be631eefbfc86</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T16:15:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest--ba93eb6e2f1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest" /><summary type="html">Germany’s far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party headed towards a landslide victory in state ​elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in its bid to form the country's first far-right state government since World War II. However, final results showed AfD falling three seats short of an absolute majority, with 39 lawmakers in an 83-member parliament.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Nepal rescue operations, World Nomad Games and Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e7cfe1963ca27fe2a39b8dc5ac64f6c92a01d50b418594df5553def171f28f</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T14:21:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv--d0868f737f26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">From the desperate search for workers trapped in the hydropower tunnels buried by the catastrophic flooding in Nepal to crowds of women mourning the victims of a US bombardment of a wedding in southern Iran, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'A bad sign': US envoys head to Kyiv after three-hour talks with Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d8f7b7e69ecbbfaab646b241ee6970c850daf5517a871dcac6f2efd1b50a74e</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T06:18:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-bad-sign-us-envoys-head-to-kyiv-after-three-hour-talks-with-putin--ef402e9abb2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-bad-sign-us-envoys-head-to-kyiv-after-three-hour-talks-with-putin" /><summary type="html">As US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner head to Kyiv following what the White House described as "substantive" talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin, FRANCE 24 correspondent Gulliver Cragg talks about what he describes as a climate of scepticism in Ukraine that these latest negotiations could bring a long-awaited breakthrough.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD eyes historic state victory in Saxony-Anhalt election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:548c5efe933a6ab0b29b218538aa4053083b13e906d6aaeed878929a43767805</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:52:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-eyes-historic-state-victory-in-saxony-anhalt-election--d84eb1b6b427.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-eyes-historic-state-victory-in-saxony-anhalt-election" /><summary type="html">Germany's anti-immigrant Alternative for Germany party is aiming to become the first far-right party to take power at a state level since World War II as voters in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt head to the polls Sunday. However, a failure to secure an absolute majority may see the politically isolated party struggle to form a government.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>After meeting with US envoys in Kyiv, Zelensky says war likely to ‘continue in winter’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c06d4b512dca6bdd1abec711aa1383377d02b758ba785c4ff46ae15495a44ae</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T04:57:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-live-trump-s-envoys-head-to-ukraine-after-substantive-talks-with-putin--f41091ccbfca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-live-trump-s-envoys-head-to-ukraine-after-substantive-talks-with-putin" /><summary type="html">Although Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky described talks with US special envoy Steve Witkoff and Donald Trump’s son-in-law Jared Kushner as “substantial”, he warned that the war with Russia was likely to continue this winter. The US envoys arrived in Kyiv for their first official visit on Sunday, a day after meeting Russia’s President Vladimir Putin in Moscow. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Witkoff: Putin's messenger?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5708bcb016af62bb356331297a8077c6e7ac1489173a9772d13a2bad7620e097</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T18:02:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260905-witkoff-putin-s-messenger--1b668b4d5419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260905-witkoff-putin-s-messenger" /><summary type="html">What did Steve Witkoff know about Russia when he was first sent to see President Vladimir Putin in February of last year?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Two senior Reform UK officials resign as Farage faces fresh foreign donations scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1499cb3f52c23f24c82e418db6cd74431098db4da58f14f28d18bbfef8014714</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:30:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-two-senior-reform-uk-officials-resign-as-farage-faces-fresh-foreign-donations-scandal--c43eb44d3d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-two-senior-reform-uk-officials-resign-as-farage-faces-fresh-foreign-donations-scandal" /><summary type="html">Two senior officials from the hard-right Reform UK party stepped down Friday following a hidden-camera investigation that appeared to show them soliciting substantial foreign funding for party-commissioned opinion polls and a potential £500,000 donation from a US donor – banned under UK law.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Putin orders 72-hour halt in strikes on Kyiv as Trump envoys arrive in Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a0496d902d05df49a8a03a4111f061b07c85df125e1e5e7a1d4ae0c1bfd64bf</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T02:37:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-and-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-the-war--2b81279000c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-and-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-the-war" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Saturday ordered a 72-hour pause in strikes on Kyiv as US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrived in Moscow. The visit is part of renewed efforts to end the war in Ukraine, and the two men are set to travel to Kyiv on Sunday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Major potential breaches of British election law': Inside Channel 4’s investigation into Reform UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d74eefb57a04a996b76ba57935752f39d24056d07c11c281d9aea12af306a3e7</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:52:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-major-potential-breaches-of-british-election-law-understanding-channel-4-s-investigation--100a26e41120.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-major-potential-breaches-of-british-election-law-understanding-channel-4-s-investigation" /><summary type="html">Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Peter Geoghegan, an award-winning investigative journalist. He's the editor of the Substack Democracy for Sale and the author of the best-selling book "Democracy for Sale". Geoghegan explains the significance of the Channel 4 investigation into Reform UK, not simply over the conduct allegedly captured on camera, but in the broader question of how political influence is financed and made visible, or invisible, within British democracy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>German power grid sabotage attack linked to ‘climate extremism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:694da36134db6b1893df99034dcee01c332669bbc96630c858ae40db1bbabed8</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:40:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism--b5a9f0391572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt on Friday said the evidence in a recent spate of sabotage attacks on power grids across the country points to a militant climate activist.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's 'most dangerous man': A PR gift for the AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3c74bd712e4eaf51604d024777b88e83df5ab6d49ec4095d3883b8b18725dff</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:31:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd--f852f5df9336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd" /><summary type="html">This week, the Ukrainian capital was hit by Russia's most intense wave of air attacks on Kyiv, reportedly in four years, with Reuters describing air raid sirens, drones, cruise and ballistic missiles exhausting Ukraine’s defence system, with 12 people killed and the Ukrainian foreign minister making a direct appeal to Western allies for more Patriot interceptor missiles.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>'Italian opposition fragmented: No alternative leader, no other possible leader than Giorgia Meloni'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f52e920a61688b156df64f7d2b9ba87c64e65f87108272a873450f9008978ce</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-m--1c36e6864261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-meloni-1" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Political analyst Lorenzo Pregliasco, co-founder of polling agency YouTrend and adjunct professor at the University of Bologna. He argues that Giorgia Meloni’s unusual longevity in office is best understood not simply as a record of political strength, but as the product of a carefully calibrated governing strategy. Meloni has maintained stability partly by avoiding structural reforms disruptive enough to mobilize multiple constituencies against her at once. Her dominance within Fratelli d’Italia, the absence of a credible alternative leader, and a fragmented opposition have reinforced that advantage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider, the ideologist behind the AFD’s plans in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5563bd0ce66277997a997d82fe5a4b99581970c5968a014541e30aa42e4c28f</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt--220beb71b19c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt" /><summary type="html">The far-right German political party Alternative for Germany could win a historical victory in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt in key elections this Sunday. The party’s agenda is more radical than ever and inspired by the proposals of an influential ideologist in the region: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France announces €1 billion aid for farmers after climate-hit summer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aae5509176d003486243db340befada2c14262457cd0701a370c2a545dfb98c</id><updated>2026-09-08T04:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:12:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-_1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer--e6ed56d5d705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-%E2%82%AC1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer" /><summary type="html">France has recorded its hottest summer on record this year as the country battled heatwaves, drought and massive wildfires. The extreme weather has continued into September, with France's national weather service placing five departments on orange alert for several days. Temperatures are expected to reach 40°C in some areas. France's agriculture minister also announced a plan to unlock over 1 billion euros in aid to the agriculture sector, which has been severely affected by the extreme weather.</summary></entry></feed>
